<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abd al-Haqq II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1419–1465</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abd al-Haqq II was the last Marinid sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, proclaimed as a baby in 1420 and kept under the control of Wattasid regents for most of his reign. In 1459 he tried to free himself by massacring the Wattasids, but his government grew unpopular, and he was killed in a revolt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> in 1465. The surviving Wattasids later founded their own sultanate.</p></div>
